! mcp_bootstrap_p154.strap -- the tail of the ERASE LONG GAP / WRITE
! set-up path (E WR31), the four tape-table INDEX SYNs, and the whole
! of the CHANGE DENSITY routine (K DENST), printed page 154.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.161.  The header was READ and not
! assumed: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP
! CARD ID IB000046   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  154", and
! the column-heading row's own "LOCATION 217657" names line 1's word.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FORTY-EIGHT PRINTED LINES.  Thirty-seven carry a LOCATION:
! thirty-three emit bits and four are SYNs (lines 23, 25, 26, 28),
! which print a location and a data description and deposit nothing.
! Eleven lines carry nothing at all -- line 15 is a CNOP that found
! the counter already on a word boundary, lines 24 and 27 are
! comment cards, and lines 29-36 are the DENSITY banner box.
!
! Two routines, back to back, with a definitions block between:
!
!   lines 1-22   the tail of the tape WRITE set-up.  Line 1's SIC/
!                line 2's B are the return of the CHANGE MODE
!                routine that printed p.152 line 48 labels K K MODE;
!                the page then tests S MULTI and S ELG, issues an
!                ERASE LONG GAP CTL command (line 8, the ",46."
!                operand is decimal 46 = 0o56 and the listing's
!                second half word prints 000056.15), waits for end
!                of op, and at E WR31 (line 13) plants the control-
!                word address into the WRITE instruction at E WR311
!                (line 18) with an SVA.  Line 21 turns on the write
!                bit in the unit status table and line 22 returns to
!                K SUPP.
!   lines 23-28  FOUR INDEX SYNs -- E A, E F, E X, E U -- naming
!                index registers 12, 13, 8 and 11.  >>> THEY ARE
!                WRITTEN AS WORD ADDRESSES, "SYN,12.0", NOT AS
!                "SYN,$12", AND THAT IS WHAT THE LOCATION COLUMN
!                SAYS: 000014.00 is word 0o14 = 12. <<<  See THE
!                ASSEMBLER LIMITATION below; this is the first page
!                in the corpus that discriminates the two spellings.
!   lines 37-48  K DENST, the CHANGE DENSITY routine.  It loads the
!                caller's density code out of index word $0 bit 17
!                (line 37), compares it against S SET DN / S U DENS,
!                returns through S RET AD if the density is already
!                right, and otherwise writes 0o36 (high) or 0o37
!                (low) into the density-op command word that printed
!                p.155 labels K DEN OP at 217707.00.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CARD-SERIAL COLUMN -- NOTHING FELL OFF EITHER END
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The serials run IB000046 (line 1) to IB000086 (line 48), read off
! the right-hand band at 600 dpi.  Line 1's serial IS the header's
! own CARD ID, so nothing fell off the top.  SEVEN serials are
! printed twice -- one card carrying two statements:
!
!   IB000046  lines  1, 2   SIC,K K MODE        ; B,K MODE
!   IB000050  lines  6, 7   LX,0,$+1.0          ; SX,0,S IO INS($12)
!   IB000052  lines  9,10   LVI,1,$+1.0         ; B,M IO REJ
!   IB000053  lines 11,12   SIC,K EOP R         ; B,K SEOP T
!   IB000057  lines 16,17   LX,0,$+1.0          ; SX,0,S IO INS($12)
!   IB000059  lines 19,20   LVI,1,$+1.0         ; B,M IO REJ
!   IB000080  lines 41,42   LV,1,S RET AD($12)  ; B,1.0($1)
!
! 48 lines - 7 doubled = 41 cards = IB000086 - IB000046 + 1.  Both
! SIC/branch pairs are complete on this page, so the page-break
! straddle of docs/transcription_workflow.md does not arise and no
! row is left out of the deck.
!
! Note the CARD ID PREFIX HAS CHANGED: printed p.152 runs IA000047
! ..IA000092.  Somewhere in printed p.153 the volume rolls over to
! IB, and printed p.154 opens at IB000046.
!
! >>> THE SURVEY IS WRONG ABOUT THIS PAGE, TWICE. <<<
! strap/mcp_survey.py reported 26 rows, a first location of
! "176606.00", and THREE trailing-"+" rows.  The truth is 33
! emitting rows plus 4 SYNs, a first location of 217657.40, and
! FOUR trailing-"+" rows (lines 23, 25, 26 and 28 -- it lost E F or
! E X).  "176606" is not a misreading of any location printed on
! this page; 217657.40 is line 1's own LOCATION and the heading
! row's own LOCATION field reads 217657 beside it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOINS -- BOTH SIDES CLOSED, NEITHER BY THIS PAGE'S INK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE PAGE PRINTS NO SLC, SO NO !CHECK BELOW CAN TEST THE
! ORIGIN. <<<  A hard SLC overrides the arriving counter silently
! (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "A HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE WITH
! THE ARRIVING COUNTER").  It is nevertheless fixed four ways, and
! three of them never touch this page's ink:
!
!   (a) THE HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION 217657", printed by IBM's
!       assembler at the right-hand end of the column-heading line
!       and read, not assumed.  It gives the word and not the bit.
!   (b) NEAR SIDE.  The volume OCR of PDF p.160 -- printed p.153, a
!       DIFFERENT page and therefore an admissible witness -- ends
!       at its line 48: "4&% 217657.CC OCCCO3.C3 O01  LVI,1,S IO
!       MOD  -IF IOC NULL, USE STANDARD MCDE".  An LVI is a HALF
!       word at 217657.00, so it leaves the counter at exactly
!       217657.40, which is this page's line 1.
!   (c) FAR SIDE.  The volume OCR of PDF p.162 -- printed p.155 --
!       opens "1* 217704.40 C.37 8B OC10C0.36 FO  CMLILL(BL,1),S
!       SET UP($11)".  Line 48 here is a HALF word at 217704.00 and
!       so leaves the counter at exactly 217704.40.
!   (d) TWO OUTSIDE PAGES PIN TWO OF THIS PAGE'S OWN LABELS, and
!       they pin the counter THROUGH the page and not only at its
!       ends:
!         E WR31 at 217667.00 -- printed p.153 line 43 prints
!           "217654.40  217667.10 00  B,E WR31" and its line 45
!           prints "217655.40  217667.32 C2  BXE,E WR31"; another
!           page prints "217637.00  217667.10 00  B,E WR31" (OCR
!           line 7972).  A plain B prints target+.10, so E WR31 is
!           the EVEN half word of 217667.  This deck's counter
!           reaches it after twelve emitting rows.
!         K DENST at 217674.40 -- FIVE other pages print
!           "B,K DENST" against "217674.50 00" (OCR lines 8129,
!           8397, 8423, 8445, 9430).  A plain B prints target+.10,
!           so K DENST is the ODD half word of 217674.  This deck's
!           counter reaches it after twenty-two emitting rows and
!           four SYNs.
!       A wrong origin moves both together, and both are printed
!       on pages this deck does not read.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THE ASSEMBLER LIMITATION -- FIVE ROWS ARE LEFT FAILING,
! >>> AND ALL FIVE ARE ONE BUG. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! strap_asm puts a symbol's or an operand's RAW BIT VALUE into
! three fields that real STRAP fills with the WORD NUMBER.  This
! page is the first in the landed corpus that can tell the two
! apart, and that was CHECKED, not assumed:
!
!   * INDEX AND J.  Every index-register SYN in a landed deck is
!     spelled "$N" -- printed pp.45 and 46 carry "QX INN SYN,$1",
!     printed p.48 carries "L IODX SYN,$3" through "L WORKX
!     SYN,$10", printed p.61 carries "T X1 SYN,$10".  strap_asm's
!     sys_alias path covers that spelling.  MCP's own source uses
!     BOTH conventions and printed p.154 is the first LANDED page
!     to use the other one.
!   * THE I/O THIRD OPERAND.  Grepped across decks/: every nonzero
!     third operand on a CTL/RD/W/LOC/REL in the corpus is written
!     BARE, and the only dotted ones are zero.  The nearest case is
!     printed p.16 line 35, "X11 3 CTL(SEOP),0.0($15),(8)137"
!     against "000137.15 00" -- RENDERED at 600 dpi to be sure, and
!     THE PAGE REALLY DOES PRINT IT WITH NO TRAILING PERIOD, so
!     that deck is faithful and passes honestly.  printed p.154
!     line 8 is the first landed row with a dotted nonzero one.
!
! The four cards on lines 23-28 name index registers BY WORD
! ADDRESS, "E U  SYN,11.0", and the LOCATION column confirms it:
! the page prints 000013.00+ for E U, which is word 0o13 = 11, bit
! 0 -- bit address 704.  Real STRAP then uses E U in an INDEX field
! and in a J field and gets register 11 (byte 8B).
!
! strap_asm takes the index/J field as the symbol's BIT value & 0xF,
! which for 704 is 0, so FOUR ROWS ASSEMBLE WITH INDEX/J = 0:
!
!     line  4  BZBZ,S ELG(EU)          000000.62 80  (printed 8B)
!     line 13  LV,$8,S CW ADR(EA)      000003.60 30  (printed 3C)
!     line 14  SVA,EX,E WR311+.32      217671.41 D0  (printed .61)
!     line 21  CM1111,S WR(EU)         000000.72 80  (printed 8B)
!
! AND THE SAME BUG IN A THIRD FIELD, LINE 8.  The I/O operation's
! third operand is a WORD quantity: the page prints
! "CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),46." (a trailing period, read at 1200 dpi,
! the same baseline dot as the one in "0.0") against
! "000056.15 00", and 0o56 is 46 -- the operand's WORD number.
! strap_asm puts 46 words = 2944 bits in the field:
!
!     line  8  CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),46.  000000.00 8E 005600.15 00
!                                      (printed 000056.15 00, and
!                                       0o5600 is exactly 46 * 64)
!
! Measured, varying only that operand:
!
!     46.      005600.15 00     the PRINTED form, FAILS
!     (8)56.   005600.15 00     the same quantity in octal, FAILS
!     46       000056.15 00     passes, but says 46 BITS
!     (8)56    000056.15 00     passes, but says 0o56 BITS
!
! The bare spellings pass by putting the right NUMBER in the field
! for the wrong REASON, so the printed form is written and the row
! is left failing.  printed p.155 line 18 prints
! "CTL,0.0($14),(8)176." against "000176.05 00" (volume OCR of PDF
! p.162) -- 0o176 is again the WORD number -- SO THE NEXT PAGE'S
! TRANSCRIBER WILL HIT THIS EXACT ROW.  That is the falsifiable
! part: if p.155 line 18 assembles to 000176.05 with the printed
! form, this diagnosis is wrong.
!
! THE PRINTED FORM IS WRITTEN AND THESE ROWS ARE LEFT FAILING,
! per docs/transcription_workflow.md and the brief: a substitution
! would be self-contradictory here, because the SAME CARD'S !SYM
! independently checks the printed value.  Measured, with the four
! SYNs rewritten "EU SYN,$11" and nothing else changed:
!
!     EA at 000014.00   assembled bit 1792, listing bit 768   FAIL
!     EU at 000013.00   assembled bit 1728, listing bit 704   FAIL
!     the four index/J rows above                             PASS
!
! i.e. it trades four wrong bytes (the index/J four; line 8 is a
! different field and the $N rewrite does not touch it) for four
! wrong SYMBOL TABLE ENTRIES, which is strictly worse -- the merge carries the symbol
! table.  "EU SYN,11" (no dot, an integer) makes the bytes pass too
! and puts 11 BITS in the table, which prints 000000.13 and is
! equally wrong.
!
! THE DIAGNOSIS, stated so it can be killed: these fields want the
! operand's WORD NUMBER, value // 64 -- masked to four bits for an
! index or a J, unmasked for the I/O count.  That one rule explains
! every case the corpus has:
!     $11       -> word 27 -> 27 & 15 = 11   (today's sys_alias
!                                             path gets this right)
!     E U=704   -> word 11 -> 11 & 15 = 11   (today: 704 & 15 = 0)
!     T IXF     -> word 26 -> 26 & 15 = 10   (strap_asm.py ~2498
!                                             records exactly this
!                                             failure, fixed by the
!                                             alias special case)
!     46.       -> word 46 -> 46 = 0o56        (today: 2944)
!     (8)176.   -> word 126 -> 126 = 0o176     (printed p.155 l.18)
! Printed p.154 is, as far as the landed corpus goes, the FIRST
! page that discriminates them, because it is the first to SYN an
! index register by word value instead of by "$N".  Nothing was
! written under strap/ for this deck.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS -- WHAT WAS SETTLED AND ON WHAT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This page opens round glyphs constantly (its own heading prints
! "LOCATICN" and "BINARY CUTPUT", and every ".00" prints ".CC").  A
! round glyph in a LOCATION or an OCTAL BINARY field is a 0 with
! certainty.  The rest:
!
! (1) LINE 4 IS "BZBZ", NOT "BZRZ", AND LINE 43 IS "BZRZ", NOT
!     "BZBZ" -- ON ONE PAGE.  Both print a worn middle glyph.  The
!     BYTES separate them and so does the shape of the instruction:
!     line 4 is a branch-on-bit with an operand and prints
!     "...34 04", which is BZBZ (printed p.152 line 24 measured
!     BZB 00 / BZBZ 04 / BZBN 08 / BZB1 0C / BB1 0E); line 43 is a
!     bare indicator branch and prints "217702.74 C0", which is
!     BZRZ (printed p.152 line 14 measured BZRZ C0 against BRZ C2).
!     At 1200 dpi line 4's third glyph is a closed-bowl B and line
!     43's has the open leg of an R.
! (2) "S SET DN" AND "S U DENS" ARE CONFIRMED FROM OUTSIDE, which is
!     what makes their D's safe: printed p.99 line 31 defines
!     S SET DN SYN(BU,1),0.33 (= 0o41) and line 36 defines S U DENS
!     SYN(BU,1),0.49 (= 0o61), and lines 38, 39 and 47 here print
!     exactly 000000.41 and 000000.61.  Address agreement, not ink.
! (3) THE ROUTINE NAMES ARE SETTLED BY THEIR OWN ENGLISH.  The
!     banner on line 30 reads DENSITY and the comment cards read
!     "(UNIT DENSITY SET TO DESIRED DENSITY)"; line 44's comment is
!     "-HIGH DENSITY DESIRED" and line 46's is "-LOW DENSITY
!     DESIRED".  So K DENST, Z CH DEN and K LOW D are DENSITY SET,
!     CHANGE DENSITY and LOW DENSITY.  K DENST is also spelled out
!     in the calling-sequence card on line 33 and is referenced by
!     five other pages.
! (4) LINES 6 AND 16 PRINT THE SAME STATEMENT, "LX,0,$+1.0", and
!     lines 9 and 19 print the same statement, "LVI,1,$+1.0" --
!     each pair in the same character positions off the same drum.
!     The trailing glyph after the dot is an open round in all four
!     and it sits in a BIT-OFFSET field, which can only hold an
!     octal digit, so it is a 0.  (Printed p.152 line 42 writes the
!     same instruction as "LX,0,$+1." with nothing after the dot;
!     this page writes the 0.  Both assemble identically.)
! (5) LINE 9 CARRIES AN INK SPECK about four character cells to the
!     right of its statement, above the baseline.  It is not a
!     character: line 19 prints the identical statement with clean
!     paper there, and the two rows compile the same word.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK -- A NINTH THING IT IS NOT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every LINE NUMBER on this page is followed by an asterisk; that
! is the ordinary line-number column.  ONE row carries a SECOND
! asterisk, in the LOCATION column: line 19, "217672.00 *".
!
! This page supplies the strongest kind of evidence about it that
! docs/transcription_workflow.md's ladder knows -- THE SAME
! STATEMENT PRINTED TWICE ON ONE PAGE.  Lines 9 and 19 are both
! "LVI,1,$+1.0", both compile target+.03 with byte 01, both sit on
! an even half word, and both are the first statement of a doubled
! card whose second statement is "B,M IO REJ".  Line 19 carries the
! asterisk and line 9 does not.  So the asterisk is not a property
! of the statement, of the operation, of the byte, of the half-word
! parity, or of being the first statement on a two-statement card.
! RECORDED AND NOT EXPLAINED.  No rule is proposed from one page.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE EXTERNALS.  Every one is already carried at this value by a
! LANDED deck, and every citation below is a DIFFERENT printed page
! -- none of them is this page reading itself.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! K K MODE 217624.40  printed p.152 line 48 is the label row,
!                     "K K MODE  B,$", and SIC prints the BARE
!                     24-bit address with no operation bits, so
!                     line 1 here pins it TO THE BIT.
KKMODE  SYN, (8)217624.40
! K MODE   217615.00  printed p.152 line 35 is the label row,
!                     "K MODE  SV,1,$L"; three other pages print
!                     "B,K MODE" against "217615.10 00".  Line 2 is
!                     a plain branch: half word only.
KMODE   SYN, (8)217615.0
! S MULTI  000000.33  printed p.99 line 24 "-MULTI-UNIT CHAN";
!                     decks p.99, p.122, p.123 and p.124 carry
!                     0.27 (= 0o33).  Line 3 pins the bit.
SMULTI  SYN(BU,1), 0.27
! S ELG    000000.62  printed p.99 line 41 "-ERASE LONG GAP"; deck
!                     p.99 carries 0.50 (= 0o62).  Line 4 pins the
!                     bit, and line 8's comment on this page is
!                     "-ERASE LONG GAP COMMAND".
SELG    SYN(BU,1), 0.50
! S IO INS 000004.00  printed p.101 line 17 "-IO INSTR. LAST";
!                     decks p.101, p.122, p.135 and p.152 carry
!                     4.0.  Lines 7 and 17 pin the half word.
SIOINS  SYN(BU,64), 4.0
! M IOREJ  221261.00  deck p.135 line 25 carries it.  Lines 10 and
!                     20 are plain branches: half word only.
MIOREJ  SYN, (8)221261.0
! K EOP R  221354.40  printed p.160's label row (OCR line 9654,
!                     "221354.40  221354.74 C2  K EOP R  BRZ,$")
!                     and four pages printing "SIC,K EOP R" against
!                     "221354.40 80".  Line 11 is a SIC, so it pins
!                     K EOP R TO THE BIT.
KEOPR   SYN, (8)221354.40
! K SEOP T 221350.40  two other pages print "B,K SEOP T" against
!                     "221350.50 00" (OCR 8022, 8259).  Line 12 is
!                     a plain branch: half word only.
KSEOPT  SYN, (8)221350.40
! S CW ADR 000003.40  printed p.101 line 14 "-CONTROL WORD
!                     ADDRESS"; decks p.101 and p.151 carry
!                     SYN(BU,18),3.32 (= 000003.40).  Line 13 pins
!                     the bit (its printed .60 is .40 plus J=8's
!                     .20).
SCWADR  SYN(BU,18), 3.32
! S WR     000000.72  printed p.99 line 46 "-WRITE, OPERATION
!                     STATUS"; decks p.99, p.122 and p.127 carry
!                     0.58 (= 0o72).  Line 21 pins the bit.
SWR     SYN(BU,1), 0.58
! K SUPP   216242.00  printed p.128 line 3 is the label row,
!                     "K SUPP  NOP,K COMM R"; eleven landed decks
!                     carry it.  Line 22 is a plain branch: half
!                     word only.
KSUPP   SYN, (8)216242.0
! S SET DN 000000.41  printed p.99 line 31 "-ORIGINAL DENSITY SET";
!                     deck p.99 carries 0.33 (= 0o41).  Line 38
!                     pins the bit.
SSETDN  SYN(BU,1), 0.33
! S U DENS 000000.61  printed p.99 line 36 "-CURRENT DENSITY OF
!                     UNIT"; deck p.99 carries 0.49 (= 0o61).
!                     Lines 39 and 47 pin the bit.
SUDENS  SYN(BU,1), 0.49
! S RET AD 000005.00  printed p.101 line 18 "-RETURN ADDRESS IN
!                     MCP"; decks p.101, p.129 and p.135 carry
!                     SYN(BU,19),5.0.  Line 41 pins the half word
!                     (its printed .02 is J=1's own bits).
SRETAD  SYN(BU,19), 5.0
! K DEN OP 217707.00  printed p.155 line 5 is the LABEL ROW -- the
!                     volume OCR of PDF p.162 reads "-* 2177C7.CCO
!                     CCCCCO.CO BE 000000.C5 CC  K CEN CP
!                     CTL,0.0($14),0.0  -CHANGE DENSITY COMMAND".
!                     A different page, so an admissible witness.
!                     Line 48 is an SVA to K DEN OP+.32 and prints
!                     217707.43, whose .40 is the half-word select;
!                     the bit WITHIN the half word is unobservable
!                     (docs/transcription_workflow.md, WHAT THE
!                     ORACLE CANNOT SEE, item 1), and ".00" here is
!                     a convention backed by p.155's label row, not
!                     a reading.
KDENOP  SYN, (8)217707.0

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN.  The page prints NO SLC.  217657.40 is line 1's own
! printed LOCATION and 217657 is the heading row's own "LOCATION"
! field; see THE JOINS for the witnesses that never touch this
! page's ink.  Stated hard so the deck assembles standalone, which
! ASSERTS it rather than checking it.  Written in printed octal,
! per docs/transcription_workflow.md's "(8)NNNN.FF" rule.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)217657.40

! ---- tail of the tape WRITE set-up -------------------------------
        SIC,KKMODE                   ! line  1
        B,KMODE                      ! line  2  (same card as 1)
        BZB,SMULTI($10),EWR31        ! line  3  -IF SINGLE UNIT 0, PROCEED TO RD
        BZBZ,SELG(EU),EWR31          ! line  4  -GO TO SET UP WRITE IF NOT ELG
        CNOP                         ! line  5  (emits 000000.30 00)
        LX,0,$+1.0                   ! line  6
        SX,0,SIOINS($12)             ! line  7  (same card as 6)
        CTL(SEOP),0.0($14),46.       ! line  8  -ERASE LONG GAP COMMAND
        LVI,1,$+1.0                  ! line  9
        B,MIOREJ                     ! line 10  (same card as 9)
        SIC,KEOPR                    ! line 11
        B,KSEOPT                     ! line 12  (same card as 11) -CHECK FOR INDICATORS
EWR31   LV,$8,SCWADR(EA)             ! line 13
        SVA,EX,EWR311+.32            ! line 14  -CTW AD. IN WRITE INST.
        CNOP                         ! line 15  (emits NOTHING: line 14's SVA is a
                                     !           half word landing the counter on
                                     !           217670.00, already aligned)
        LX,0,$+1.0                   ! line 16
        SX,0,SIOINS($12)             ! line 17  (same card as 16)
EWR311  W,0.0($14),0.0               ! line 18
        LVI,1,$+1.0                  ! line 19
        B,MIOREJ                     ! line 20  (same card as 19)
        CM1111,SWR(EU)               ! line 21  -TURN ON WRITE BIT IN U.S.T.
        B,KSUPP                      ! line 22

! ---- the four tape-table index SYNs ------------------------------
! PRINTED FORM, IN PRINTED ORDER.  Each prints a LOCATION that is a
! WORD address (000014.00 = word 12) and a data description of
! "+00000000  NULL".  They deposit nothing: line 22 leaves the
! counter at 217674.40 and line 37 is printed there.
EA      SYN, 12.0                    ! line 23  -UNIT AREA TABLE INDEX
                                     ! line 24  comment card: "$10   -CHANNEL STATUS TABLE INDEX"
EF      SYN, 13.0                    ! line 25  -FILE AREA TABLE INDEX
EX      SYN, 8.0                     ! line 26  -SCRATCH INDEX
                                     ! line 27  comment card: "$9    SCRATCH INDEX"
EU      SYN, 11.0                    ! line 28  -UNIT STATUS TABLE INDEX
! >>> AND NOTE THE NAME "E X" COLLIDES WITH THE "EX" MNEMONIC in
! opcodes.MISC_CODES.  It does no harm here -- no row on this page
! is an EX instruction, and "SVA,EX,..." is parsed as a J operand,
! not as an operation -- so THE COLLISION IS UNTESTED BY THIS PAGE.
! Recorded because that is the shape of the T IXF bug at
! strap_asm.py ~2498: a name that only misbehaves once some OTHER
! page, merged beside this one, writes the operation.

! ---- *****DENSITY***** -------------------------------------------
! lines 29-36 are comment cards: the banner box and the calling
! sequence.  They are recorded in THE PRINTED LISTING below.
KDENST  L(BU,1),$0.17,46             ! line 37
        BZB1,SSETDN($11),ZCHDEN      ! line 38
        KF(BU,1),SUDENS($11),46      ! line 39
        BZAE,ZCHDEN                  ! line 40
        LV,1,SRETAD($12)             ! line 41
        B,1.0($1)                    ! line 42  (same card as 41) -IF SO, RETURN
ZCHDEN  BZRZ,KLOWD                   ! line 43
        LVI,1,(8)36.                 ! line 44  -HIGH DENSITY DESIRED
        B,$+1.0                      ! line 45
KLOWD   LVI,1,(8)37.                 ! line 46  -LOW DENSITY DESIRED
        ST(BU,1),SUDENS($11),46      ! line 47
        SVA,1,KDENOP+.32             ! line 48

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, AS RENDERED AT 300/600/900/1200 dpi
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The separator on lines 32 and 33 is the IBM RECORD MARK, a
! vertical stroke with two crossbars, read at 1200 dpi.  It is
! written here as "++" because the deck is ASCII.  (Printed p.152
! line 32 prints the SAME glyph and decks/mcp_bootstrap_p152.strap
! transcribes it as ";" -- cosmetic, inside a comment card, and not
